model {
  extend basalt.modelGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Request reliability counts only the retained local model and gateway sources. Explicit purpose records match the exact pool, source and hashed client key; unclassified keys count as real. Proof counts remain visible separately, while token and cost totals retain every request. The same bounded SQL read supplies the overview and rolling one-hour and twenty-four-hour success objectives. Empty real traffic has no success rate. Optional reliability reads use a savepoint so an unavailable monitor cannot discard the usage, token or cost answers. Availability RPC failure retains an independently measured reliability verdict and both closed failure classes. An inactive, stale, lagging or unclassified capture cannot establish the objective. The once-per-minute availability check-in reports only the synthetic pool probe. Real-request success below 99 percent emits its own error through the existing observability route. Collection unavailability remains unknown in the interface and emits only a closed Worker warning with bounded counts and reason. It creates no issue event or availability error, so issue notification rules cannot page on unknown collection. Empty real traffic and proof-only failures do not report an outage. Counts and closed reasons leave the service; keys and request content do not."
      constraint "The traffic-purpose schema is an additive named model-history migration applied only through the private reviewed schema operation. It never rewrites request history. Purpose changes use the private operations entrypoint with a dry run listing exact retained request identifiers, current classifications and an evidence hash. Applying requires the digest of that selection; a changed selection refuses. A started local receipt prevents replay after an unknown apply outcome. Restoring a proof key to real uses the same reviewed path. Public app and model routes cannot change purpose."
    }
  }
  basalt.telemetry -[sync]-> basalt.pool "read request reliability contracts for monitor diagnostics"
}
